spans.s:
átas, adv.
 —1. (as abl. of pron. root a [1098],
and synonymous w. asmāt) from it; so 22^9,
sc. paṅkāt; ato ‘nya, other than it, 68^12;
 —2. from this (place), 83^15;
 —3. from this
(time), 96^21; cf. ūrdhvam; then, 40^16;
 —4.
from this (cause), 35^10; therefore, 27^8, etc.;
w. correl. yatas, 36^3; hence; and so, 39^4,
42^21; so then, 73^12. [pron. root a, 502.]
